I had one of those LA36 Decwriters and only recently threw out its
rusting hulk.

If I can remember correctly, the Decwriter and some of the AJ matrix
printers were not actually a "matrix" printer, rather a "vector"
printer.  The printing was accomplished by a 1 x 7 matrix of little
hammers which would fire into a ribbon.  Typically, a character could
not have adjacent horizontal dots as the hammer could not retract and
strike again in the time it took the printer to advance that width
(say 1/6 of a character).  As the electromagents and hammers got
faster, it was possible to have printers which approached 1200 baud.


