I must be thinking of different printers. I think there
were some that had staggered dots so overlapping could
be achieved both vertically and horizontally.

Perhaps it was the Apple printer I'm thinking of.
This bizarre machine printed slower in draft mode!
Because in draft mode, although proportional
spacing was turned off at the character level,
the idiot who did the driver forgot to turn off
the proportional spacing between characters so
that the head moved forwards in hundreths of an inch
increments slowing the head to a crawl.

And as a consequence of mixing proportional spacing
with non-proportional characters, the printer was
incapable of legibly printing the phrase

"all mississippi llamas live in illinois"

