I just remembered something *related* to what you are saying:

The LA36 DECWriter used "overstrike" characters to represent some
of the APL operators. When you listed out a function definition,
these characters would print as "character one - backspace -
character two". The LA36 did *not* combine the characters into
one, but actually typed one character and then overstruck it with
the other character.


