On Dec 2, 4:28=A0pm, Chris <archive.rai...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hi. I've got an old Alphastation 200 (VMS 7.1). It has an RX23 3.5"
> floppy drive. =A0I want to read some old RX50 5.25" diskettes. =A0I've
> tried attaching an RX50 drive to the floppy cable but it's not
> recognized. =A0Would an RX33 drive work? =A0This all has to be done
> external to the system box, since it won't fit inside. That's OK, as
> long as it will work temporarily. =A0Can someone offer advice? Thanks.

5.25" devices behave differently than 3.5" ones so it won't work with
the standard VMS device driver.
The RX23 is AFAIK the only floppy drive model supported on some
Alpha's.
So there's no support for the RX33 or RX50, unless you're prepared to
write your own driver.
Hans


